The Real Asset

The runtime isn’t the moat.

The moat is the growing library of high-quality operators, benchmarks, reconstruction traces, and evaluations. As more people use the system, it becomes better at selecting and composing operators for new tasks.

Version 0.1 Success Criteria

A release is “done” when someone can:

1. Clone the repository.
2. Run one command.
3. Enter a natural-language mission.
4. Watch the runtime construct an execution graph.
5. Receive a reproducible artifact with an evaluation report.
6. Replay the mission later and inspect every transformation.

That is the smallest version that demonstrates the core idea. Every future Pantheon concept—Goal Seek, Semantic Navigation, Hammer Mole, Reconstruction, Moneybin artifacts—can plug into this architecture without changing its foundations. If we build this well, the rest of the ecosystem grows by adding operators rather than rewriting the core.